Notice for the driver semantics of `minimize::lbfgs` (the order of the stopping tests, the counting of
line-search trials, the reset after a failed search, the first trial step, the scaling of the initial matrix),
which were derived by reading SciPy's translation of L-BFGS-B. No source code of either was copied: the two-loop
recursion and the ring buffer are written independently (see the headers of `src/lbfgs/`), and the Rust control flow
is not a line-by-line translation (L-BFGS-B works in the compact representation with bounds; this crate uses the
two-loop recursion on the unconstrained path). The notice is kept because the behaviour is taken from that code and
the crate's tests replay its recorded runs.

